title: Niko5
---
Niko was at the library again, staring out the window deep in thought. He
looked troubled, his brow twitching as his finger tapped an uneven rhythm.

After your last encounter, you considered leaving him alone. He clearly
needed space. But you still had an essay to finish.

You approached quietly, yet he noticed you anyway. His narrowed eyes locked
onto you before he stretched like a waking cat.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Hey,"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He greeted you coldly before looking away again. His gaze seemed distant,
almost empty.

You gave a quiet greeting back, unsure how to approach him now. Apologizing
again would likely do nothing.

Suddenly, he snapped his head toward you, expression sharp with impatience.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I have a question to ask you,"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

His tone was firm, leaving no room for refusal.

You glanced around briefly, relieved no one seemed to notice.

You: "...Okay, what is it?"

You stretched the word slightly, confused.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "You're a Philosophy student,"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

You resisted the urge to respond sarcastically.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "What is your view on death?"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

The question caught you off guard.

You: "Are you serious?"

He responded with an impatient sigh and glare.

You realized he meant it.

You stayed quiet for a moment, thinking carefully.

-> It is nothing short of a calamity, it harms all
    <<incRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump Choice1N5>>
-> Death does not concern the living so why worry ourselves over it?
    <<jump Choice2N5>>
-> The unavoidable reality that gives meaning to life
    <<decRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump Choice3N5>>
===

title: Choice1N5
---
You: "I think death is a frightening thing. It harms everyone in its wake."

You spoke slowly, choosing your words carefully.

Niko's rigid posture softened slightly.

Soon enough, though, he returned to his usual distant demeanor, looking at
you as if you meant nothing.

<<jump EndNiko5>>
===

title: Choice2N5
---
You: "Death doesn't really concern the living. Why dwell on it and invite
fear?"

You shrugged lightly.

Niko froze for a moment, his expression unreadable, before settling back
into his usual posture.

<<jump EndNiko5>>
===

title: Choice3N5
---
You: "Death gives life meaning. It's what makes it worth living."

He studied you carefully, as if trying to determine whether you meant it.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I suppose it makes life worth preserving."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

His tone was quieter now.

Then he frowned.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "What a pretentious response."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

<<jump EndNiko5>>
===

title: EndNiko5
---
Niko shook his head slowly, unsatisfied.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Death isn't something to take lightly."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "You only say that because you don't know what it's like to be haunted
by it."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

His voice rose briefly before dropping into something quieter.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "You have no idea."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>
===
